      '<b>Nothing in mental life is accidental:</b> slips of the tongue, forgetting names, and everyday errors are meaningful — determined by unconscious motives and conflicts.',
      '<b>The dream is a wish-fulfilment:</b> every dream is a valid psychic phenomenon built up by complex intellectual activity, expressing a fulfilled (often disguised) wish.',
      '<b>Dreams are distorted by the censor:</b> the manifest dream we remember is the dream-work\'s transformation of the latent dream-thoughts, which are unacceptable to waking consciousness.',
