      '<b>Wit is a social and pleasure-bearing process:</b> wit — unlike the comic, which needs only two people — requires a third person to complete the pleasure, and serves tendentious (aggressive and sexual) aims.',
      '<b>Taboo reveals ambivalence:</b> taboo prohibitions combine the sacred and the forbidden, and express the ambivalence of emotions — as seen in totemism\'s relation to the father.',
